   "source": [
    "## §9 · API para Streamlit\n",
    "\n",
    "Cuatro funciones encapsulan todo el pipeline. Llámalas desde Streamlit en este orden:\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# Una sola vez al cargar la app:\n",
    "predictor = TraficoPredictor(model, scaler_X, scaler_y, history_df)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Por cada query del usuario:\n",
    "res        = route_by_address(origen, destino, mode=\"osm\")          # o \"sensors\"\n",
    "mapa       = plot_route_folium(res, save=False)\n",
    "preds, _   = predictor.predict_route(res[\"sensor_ids\"], datetime)\n",
    "eta        = compute_eta(res[\"sensor_ids\"], res[\"distancias_m\"], preds, tipo_elem_int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# eta[\"tiempo_total_min\"]   ← ETA en minutos\n",
    "# eta[\"velocidad_media_efectiva_kmh\"]\n",
    "# eta[\"tramos\"]             ← detalle por par de sensores\n",
    "# preds                     ← intensidad/ocupacion/carga por sensor\n",
    "# mapa._repr_html_()        ← HTML para st.components.v1.html(...)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Si una vez tengas la app pasamos esto a `inferencia_lib.py` y queda como módulo importable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## §10 · API meteorológica (Open-Meteo)\n",
    "\n",
    "Para fechas que no están en el histórico (ej. 12-mayo-2026) hay que pedir la lluvia a una API externa. Uso **Open-Meteo** porque es:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Gratis, sin API key.\n",
    "- Da forecast a 16 días vista y archivo histórico desde 1940.\n",
    "- Devuelve precipitación en mm hora a hora.\n",
    "\n",
    "Mapping a las features del modelo:\n",
    "- `precip_mm` ← precipitation (mm)\n",
    "- `llueve`    ← 1 si precip > 0\n",
    "- `lluvia_ord`← 0 (no), 1 (leve <2.5), 2 (moderada <7.5), 3 (intensa ≥7.5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import requests\n",
    "from datetime import datetime as _dt\n",
    "\n",
    "class WeatherClient:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Consulta Open-Meteo para una fecha+lugar concretos.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Selecciona automáticamente forecast (≤16 días vista) o archivo (histórico).\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    FORECAST = \"https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast\"\n",
    "    ARCHIVE  = \"https://archive-api.open-meteo.com/v1/archive\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, lat=40.4168, lon=-3.7038, timezone=\"Europe/Madrid\"):\n",
    "        self.lat = lat; self.lon = lon; self.tz = timezone\n",
    "\n",
    "    @staticmethod\n",
    "    def precip_to_lluvia_ord(p_mm):\n",
    "        if p_mm < 1e-3:  return 0\n",
    "        if p_mm < 2.5:   return 1\n",
    "        if p_mm < 7.5:   return 2\n",
    "        return 3\n",
    "\n",
    "    def get(self, dt):\n",
    "        dt = pd.Timestamp(dt)\n",
    "        today = pd.Timestamp(_dt.now().date())\n",
    "        endpoint = self.ARCHIVE if dt.normalize() < today else self.FORECAST\n",
    "        params = {\n",
    "            \"latitude\":   self.lat, \"longitude\": self.lon,\n",
    "            \"hourly\":     \"precipitation,rain,precipitation_probability,temperature_2m\",\n",
    "            \"start_date\": dt.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\"),\n",
    "            \"end_date\":   dt.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\"),\n",
    "            \"timezone\":   self.tz,\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        r = requests.get(endpoint, params=params, timeout=15)\n",
    "        r.raise_for_status()\n",
    "        h = r.json()[\"hourly\"]\n",
    "        # Buscar la hora más cercana\n",
    "        target_str = dt.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:00\")\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            i = h[\"time\"].index(target_str)\n",
    "        except ValueError:\n",
    "            i = 0\n",
    "        precip_mm = float(h[\"precipitation\"][i] or 0.0)\n",
    "        return {\n",
    "            \"precip_mm\":   precip_mm,\n",
    "            \"llueve\":      1 if precip_mm > 0 else 0,\n",
    "            \"lluvia_ord\":  self.precip_to_lluvia_ord(precip_mm),\n",
    "            \"temperatura\": float(h[\"temperature_2m\"][i] or 0.0),\n",
    "            \"prob_lluvia\": float(h[\"precipitation_probability\"][i] or 0.0),\n",
    "            \"fuente\":      \"open-meteo:\" + (\"archive\" if endpoint == self.ARCHIVE else \"forecast\"),\n",
    "        }\n",
    "\n",
    "weather = WeatherClient()\n",
    "print(\"WeatherClient listo.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test rápido: el día 12-mayo-2026 09:00 en Madrid\n",
    "demo = weather.get(\"2026-05-12 09:00\")\n",
    "print(f\"  test 2026-05-12 09:00: {demo}\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## §11 · Perfiles históricos por sensor\n",
    "\n",
    "Para fechas futuras los lags `intensidad_lag1..4`, `ocupacion_lag1..4`, `carga_lag1..4` no existen en el histórico. Se simulan con la **media histórica** del sensor a esa franja horaria + día_semana.\n",
    "\n",
    "La tabla resultante tiene clave `(sensor_id, slot_of_day, dow)`:\n",
    "- 1.069 sensores × 96 slots × 7 días ≈ 720 K filas.\n",
    "- Ocupa ~30 MB en RAM. Se cachea como pickle tras la primera ejecución (~15 s)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "PROFILES_PATH = OUTPUT_DIR / \"historical_profiles.pkl\"\n",
    "\n",
    "if PROFILES_PATH.exists():\n",
    "    historical_profiles = joblib.load(PROFILES_PATH)\n",
    "    print(f\"Perfiles cargados de {PROFILES_PATH.name}: {len(historical_profiles):,} filas\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Computando perfiles históricos por (sensor_id, slot, dow)... ~15 s\")\n",
    "    cols = [\"id\", \"datetime\", \"intensidad_trafico\", \"ocupacion\", \"carga\"]\n",
    "    parts = [pd.read_parquet(p, columns=cols, engine=\"pyarrow\")\n",
    "             for p in (TRAIN_PARQ, VAL_PARQ, TEST_PARQ)]\n",
    "    raw = pd.concat(parts, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "    raw[\"slot\"] = raw[\"datetime\"].dt.hour * 4 + raw[\"datetime\"].dt.minute // 15\n",
    "    raw[\"dow\"]  = raw[\"datetime\"].dt.dayofweek\n",
    "    historical_profiles = (raw.groupby([\"id\", \"slot\", \"dow\"])\n",
    "                              .agg(intensidad=(\"intensidad_trafico\", \"mean\"),\n",
    "                                   ocupacion =(\"ocupacion\",         \"mean\"),\n",
    "                                   carga    =(\"carga\",              \"mean\"))\n",
    "                              .reset_index())\n",
    "    joblib.dump(historical_profiles, PROFILES_PATH)\n",
    "    del raw, parts\n",
    "    print(f\"  guardados: {len(historical_profiles):,} filas\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Indexar para lookup O(1)\n",
    "PROFILE_IDX = (historical_profiles\n",
    "               .set_index([\"id\", \"slot\", \"dow\"])\n",
    "               [[\"intensidad\", \"ocupacion\", \"carga\"]]\n",
    "               .to_dict(\"index\"))\n",
    "print(f\"  diccionario PROFILE_IDX: {len(PROFILE_IDX):,} entradas\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## §12 · Predictor extendido (cualquier fecha)\n",
    "\n",
    "`predict_route_anytime(sensor_ids, datetime, weather=None, ...)`:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Si la fecha está en el histórico**: hace lookup directo (lo que ya existe en §6) — más exacto.\n",
    "- **Si la fecha está fuera del histórico**:\n",
    "  - Pide la lluvia a Open-Meteo (a menos que el usuario la sobreescriba).\n",
    "  - Construye los 12 lags y los 6 rolls a partir de los perfiles históricos del sensor.\n",
    "  - Calcula las features deterministas del datetime (slot/dow/mes).\n",
    "  - Asume **sin accidente** por defecto (puede sobreescribirse).\n",
    "\n",
    "Es un drop-in replacement: úsalo desde Streamlit y no te preocupas por la fecha."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "def _profile_lookup(sensor_id, slot, dow):\n",
    "    return PROFILE_IDX.get((int(sensor_id), int(slot) % 96, int(dow) % 7),\n",
    "                           {\"intensidad\": 0.0, \"ocupacion\": 0.0, \"carga\": 0.0})\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_features_anytime(sensor_id, dt, weather, tipo_elem, accidente=False):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Construye un dict con TODAS las columnas que necesita build_sequences()\n",
    "    para una fecha cualquiera (futura o pasada). 22 features por step × 4 steps.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    dt = pd.Timestamp(dt)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ── Lags 1..8 (necesitamos 8 para roll8) ────────────────────────────\n",
    "    samples = {}\n",
    "    for k in range(1, 9):\n",
    "        t_lag = dt - timedelta(minutes=15 * k)\n",
    "        slot = t_lag.hour * 4 + t_lag.minute // 15\n",
    "        dow  = t_lag.dayofweek\n",
    "        samples[k] = _profile_lookup(sensor_id, slot, dow)\n",
    "\n",
    "    feat = {}\n",
    "    for k in (1, 2, 3, 4):\n",
    "        feat[f\"intensidad_trafico_lag{k}\"] = samples[k][\"intensidad\"]\n",
    "        feat[f\"ocupacion_lag{k}\"]          = samples[k][\"ocupacion\"]\n",
    "        feat[f\"carga_lag{k}\"]              = samples[k][\"carga\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ── Rolls 4 / 8 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "    intens4 = [samples[k][\"intensidad\"] for k in (1,2,3,4)]\n",
    "    occ4    = [samples[k][\"ocupacion\"]  for k in (1,2,3,4)]\n",
    "    car4    = [samples[k][\"carga\"]      for k in (1,2,3,4)]\n",
    "    intens8 = [samples[k][\"intensidad\"] for k in range(1,9)]\n",
    "    occ8    = [samples[k][\"ocupacion\"]  for k in range(1,9)]\n",
    "    car8    = [samples[k][\"carga\"]      for k in range(1,9)]\n",
    "    feat[\"intensidad_trafico_roll4\"] = float(np.mean(intens4))\n",
    "    feat[\"intensidad_trafico_roll8\"] = float(np.mean(intens8))\n",
    "    feat[\"ocupacion_roll4\"]          = float(np.mean(occ4))\n",
    "    feat[\"ocupacion_roll8\"]          = float(np.mean(occ8))\n",
    "    feat[\"carga_roll4\"]              = float(np.mean(car4))\n",
    "    feat[\"carga_roll8\"]              = float(np.mean(car8))\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ── Contexto temporal (determinista) ────────────────────────────────\n",
    "    slot_now = dt.hour * 4 + dt.minute // 15\n",
    "    feat[\"slot_sin\"]     = float(np.sin(2 * np.pi * slot_now / 96))\n",
    "    feat[\"slot_cos\"]     = float(np.cos(2 * np.pi * slot_now / 96))\n",
    "    feat[\"dia_sem_sin\"]  = float(np.sin(2 * np.pi * dt.dayofweek / 7))\n",
    "    feat[\"dia_sem_cos\"]  = float(np.cos(2 * np.pi * dt.dayofweek / 7))\n",
    "    feat[\"mes_sin\"]      = float(np.sin(2 * np.pi * (dt.month - 1) / 12))\n",
    "    feat[\"mes_cos\"]      = float(np.cos(2 * np.pi * (dt.month - 1) / 12))\n",
    "    feat[\"es_laborable\"] = 0 if dt.dayofweek >= 5 else 1   # festivos NO considerados\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ── Lluvia (de la API) ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "    feat[\"lluvia_ord\"] = int(weather.get(\"lluvia_ord\", 0))\n",
    "    feat[\"precip_mm\"]  = float(weather.get(\"precip_mm\",  0.0))\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ── Accidente (default 0) ───────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "    if accidente:\n",
    "        feat[\"hay_accidente\"]         = 1\n",
    "        feat[\"accidente_reciente_1h\"] = 1\n",
    "        feat[\"tiempo_accidente_norm\"] = 0.5\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        feat[\"hay_accidente\"]         = 0\n",
    "        feat[\"accidente_reciente_1h\"] = 0\n",
    "        feat[\"tiempo_accidente_norm\"] = 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ── Tipo elemento ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "    feat[\"tipo_elem\"] = int(tipo_elem)\n",
    "    return feat\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def predict_route_anytime(sensor_ids, dt, weather=None, accidente=False,\n",
    "                          force_simulation=False):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Drop-in replacement de TraficoPredictor.predict_route que funciona para\n",
    "    cualquier fecha (incluso futura).\n",
    "\n",
    "    weather:           dict {lluvia_ord, precip_mm, ...} para sobreescribir API.\n",
    "    accidente:         True → simula accidente reciente en la zona.\n",
    "    force_simulation:  True → aunque dt esté en histórico, usa perfiles+API.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Devuelve (DataFrame predicciones, lista skipped, dict info).\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    dt = pd.Timestamp(dt)\n",
    "    hist_min = predictor.hist.index.get_level_values(\"datetime\").min()\n",
    "    hist_max = predictor.hist.index.get_level_values(\"datetime\").max()\n",
    "    in_hist  = (hist_min <= dt <= hist_max)\n",
    "\n",
    "    info = {\"datetime\": dt, \"in_history\": in_hist, \"force_simulation\": force_simulation}\n",
    "\n",
    "    if in_hist and not force_simulation and weather is None and not accidente:\n",
    "        # Camino rápido: lookup directo (idéntico a §6)\n",
    "        info[\"mode\"] = \"lookup_historico\"\n",
    "        preds, skipped = predictor.predict_route(sensor_ids, dt)\n",
    "        return preds, skipped, info\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Camino simulación: weather API + perfiles históricos\n",
    "    if weather is None:\n",
    "        info[\"mode\"] = \"simulacion+api_meteo\"\n",
    "        weather = weather_client_get_or_default(dt)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        info[\"mode\"] = \"simulacion+weather_manual\"\n",
    "    info[\"weather\"] = weather\n",
    "\n",
    "    rows, valid_ids, skipped = [], [], []\n",
    "    for sid in sensor_ids:\n",
    "        sid_int = int(sid)\n",
    "        # Skip si el sensor no tiene perfil histórico (raro, pero posible)\n",
    "        if (sid_int, 0, 0) not in PROFILE_IDX:\n",
    "            skipped.append(sid); continue\n",
    "        tipo = tipo_elem_int.get(sid_int, TIPO_ELEM_URB)\n",
    "        feat = build_features_anytime(sid_int, dt, weather, tipo, accidente=accidente)\n",
    "        rows.append(feat); valid_ids.append(sid_int)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if not rows:\n",
    "        return (pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"intensidad\",\"ocupacion\",\"carga\"]),\n",
    "                skipped, info)\n",
    "\n",
    "    df_rows = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "    X = build_sequences(df_rows)                                 # (N, 4, 22)\n",
    "    X_n = predictor.sX.transform(X.reshape(-1, X.shape[-1])).reshape(X.shape)\n",
    "    y_n = predictor.model.predict(X_n, verbose=0)\n",
    "    y   = predictor.sy.inverse_transform(y_n)\n",
    "    return (pd.DataFrame(y, columns=[\"intensidad\",\"ocupacion\",\"carga\"], index=valid_ids),\n",
    "            skipped, info)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def weather_client_get_or_default(dt):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Wrapper con fallback a 'sin lluvia' si la API falla.\"\"\"\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        return weather.get(dt)\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print(f\"  [aviso] Open-Meteo falló ({e}); fallback a sin lluvia.\")\n",
    "        return {\"precip_mm\": 0.0, \"llueve\": 0, \"lluvia_ord\": 0, \"fuente\": \"fallback\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"predict_route_anytime + build_features_anytime listos.\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## §13 · Demo end-to-end con fecha futura\n",
    "\n",
    "Cambia `ORIGEN_F`, `DESTINO_F`, `DATETIME_F` (cualquier fecha 1940–hoy+16 días) y vuelve a ejecutar:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ── Inputs (CUALQUIER fecha — Open-Meteo se encarga del tiempo) ────────\n",
    "ORIGEN_F   = \"Calle Valderrodrigo 31\"\n",
    "DESTINO_F  = \"NTT Data\"\n",
    "DATETIME_F = pd.Timestamp(\"2026-05-12 09:00:00\")    # martes, 09:00 → laborable\n",
    "\n",
    "# Opcional: weather=None usa API automáticamente; pasa dict para sobreescribir\n",
    "WEATHER_OVERRIDE = None        # ej: {\"lluvia_ord\": 2, \"precip_mm\": 4.0, \"llueve\": 1}\n",
    "ACCIDENTE        = False        # ej: True para simular accidente\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 78)\n",
    "print(f\"  ORIGEN   : {ORIGEN_F!r}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  DESTINO  : {DESTINO_F!r}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  DATETIME : {DATETIME_F}  (dow={DATETIME_F.day_name()})\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 78)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── 1. Routing en los dos modos ──────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "print(\"\\n[1/4] Calculando rutas...\")\n",
    "res_osm_f  = route_by_address(ORIGEN_F, DESTINO_F, mode=\"osm\")\n",
    "res_sens_f = route_by_address(ORIGEN_F, DESTINO_F, mode=\"sensors\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── 2. Mapas Folium ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "print(\"\\n[2/4] Generando mapas...\")\n",
    "m_osm_f  = plot_route_folium(res_osm_f,  filename=\"ruta_osm_futuro.html\")\n",
    "m_sens_f = plot_route_folium(res_sens_f, filename=\"ruta_sensors_futuro.html\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── 3. Predicción extendida (futuro-aware) ───────────────────────────────\n",
    "print(\"\\n[3/4] Inferencia LSTM (modo futuro)...\")\n",
    "preds_osm_f,  skip_osm_f,  info_osm  = predict_route_anytime(\n",
    "    res_osm_f[\"sensor_ids\"], DATETIME_F,\n",
    "    weather=WEATHER_OVERRIDE, accidente=ACCIDENTE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "preds_sens_f, skip_sens_f, info_sens = predict_route_anytime(\n",
    "    res_sens_f[\"sensor_ids\"], DATETIME_F,\n",
    "    weather=WEATHER_OVERRIDE, accidente=ACCIDENTE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f\"  modo OSM     : {len(preds_osm_f)} predichos / {len(skip_osm_f)} skipped  | {info_osm['mode']}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  modo SENSORS : {len(preds_sens_f)} predichos / {len(skip_sens_f)} skipped | {info_sens['mode']}\")\n",
    "if \"weather\" in info_osm:\n",
    "    w = info_osm[\"weather\"]\n",
    "    print(f\"  meteo aplicada : precip={w.get('precip_mm',0):.1f} mm  \"\n",
    "          f\"prob={w.get('prob_lluvia','?')}%  T={w.get('temperatura','?')} °C  \"\n",
    "          f\"({w.get('fuente','?')})\")\n",
    "print(f\"  lluvia_ord = {(WEATHER_OVERRIDE or info_osm.get('weather',{})).get('lluvia_ord','?')}  \"\n",
    "      f\"accidente = {ACCIDENTE}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── 4. ETA ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "print(\"\\n[4/4] Cálculo de ETA...\")\n",
    "eta_osm_f  = compute_eta(res_osm_f[\"sensor_ids\"],  res_osm_f[\"distancias_m\"],  preds_osm_f,  tipo_elem_int)\n",
    "eta_sens_f = compute_eta(res_sens_f[\"sensor_ids\"], res_sens_f[\"distancias_m\"], preds_sens_f, tipo_elem_int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Resumen ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 78)\n",
    "print(f\"  RESULTADO PARA {DATETIME_F}\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 78)\n",
    "print_eta(eta_osm_f,  header=\"MODO OSM (camino real por carretera)\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print_eta(eta_sens_f, header=\"MODO SENSORES (Dijkstra grafo de sensores)\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 78)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
